  "description": "### \ud83d\udcdc License & Mandatory Attribution (CC-BY)\nThis model is free to download and use in your projects, **provided you give clear attribution to [animalanimator.com](https://animalanimator.com/)**. \n\nThis is a life-size Akhal-Teke stallion. It has an anatomical skeleton, skinning based on anatomy, a facial system. Created with authors art + procedural tools.\nKnown for its lean, athletic build.\n\n### \ud83d\udc0e Master Equine Anatomy & Locomotion\nUsing this model for animation reference or study? Read our in-depth breakdown of horse biomechanics, skeletal structure, and gait cycles:\n\ud83d\udc49 **[The Ultimate Horse Reference for Animators](https://animalanimator.com/the-ultimate-horse-reference-for-animators/)**\n\n### \u2764\ufe0f Support on Patreon\nIf this model helps your workflow, consider supporting our work on **Patreon**! Your support allows us to keep creating free, anatomically accurate 3D wildlife assets, rigs, and educational guides for the community:\n\ud83d\udc49 **[Support us on Patreon](https://www.patreon.com/cw/AnimalAnimator)**",
